# Repository Rules and Structure

## General Description

This repository contains configuration and rules for working with Cursor IDE. It is designed to standardize development and ensure code quality.

## Repository Structure

### .cursor/
Root directory with Cursor IDE configuration

#### lsr/ (Language-Specific Rules)
Rules for specific programming languages:
- `do-erlang.md` - Rules for Erlang
- `do-flutter.md` - Rules for Flutter/Dart
- `do-javascript.md` - Rules for JavaScript
- `do-kazoo.md` - Rules for Kazoo
- `do-markdown.md` - Rules for Markdown
- `do-python.md` - Rules for Python
- `do-testing.md` - Rules for writing automated tests (pytest)
- `do-typescript.md` - Rules for TypeScript

#### skills/ (Agent Skills)
Workflow automation skills:
- `top-down-workflow/` - Steps 1–7 workflow
- `jira-sprint-planning/` - Backlog analysis and sprint planning
- `sprint-runner/` - Full sprint lifecycle
- `sprint-task-runner/` - Single sprint task end-to-end

#### rules/ (General Development Rules)
Numbered rule files:
- `00-rules.mdc` - Basic rules
- `10-requirements.mdc` - Project requirements
- `20-architecture.mdc` - Architectural principles
- `30-development.mdc` - Development rules
- `40-code-cleanup.mdc` - Code cleanup before review
- `50-observability.mdc` - Adding observability (logs, metrics)
- `60-review.mdc` - Code review rules
- `70-dev-docs.mdc` - Developer documentation
- `99-commit.mdc` - Commit rules
- `files.mdc` - File handling rules
- `makefile.mdc` - Makefile workflow conventions

#### templates/ (Templates)
Ready-made templates for various tasks:
- `top-to-bottom/roadmap.md` - Project roadmap template

## Language Guides

When working with code, you must follow the rules from the corresponding file in the `lsr/` directory:
- For Python projects read `.cursor/lsr/do-python.md`
- For TypeScript/JavaScript - `.cursor/lsr/do-typescript.md` and `.cursor/lsr/do-javascript.md`
- For Flutter/Dart - `.cursor/lsr/do-flutter.md`
- For documentation - `.cursor/lsr/do-markdown.md`
- When editing tests - `.cursor/lsr/do-testing.md`

## General Rules

The main principles of work are described in the files of the `rules/` directory. Pay special attention to:
- `files.mdc` - rules for encoding, line endings, line length
- `30-development.mdc` - development process
- `40-code-cleanup.mdc` - code cleanup before review
- `50-observability.mdc` - adding observability (logs, metrics)
- `60-review.mdc` - code review standards
